  "_gear": "the item matrix (0.00274, the developer's call; docs/item-matrix.md, shared/classGear.js): wields = the two weapon kinds the class can use (items.json kind on a weapon: sword | axe | mace | staff | dagger | scythe | crossbow | censer), wears = its one armor weight (kind on a body armor: heavy | hide | cloth); an item with `class` is that class's alone. mastery = what the class's signature items feed: key = a key of its class block, per = what one point adds (items.json mastery: 1 on its tier-3 signature, 2 on its tier-4), pct = shown as a percentage, label / labelPlural = the words.",
  "_class": "class (drafted 0.00258 under the simulator's --hero, live since 0.00267 — the developer's call, to tune in play; heavyName above names the heavy; what each kind and passive DOES is run/classes.js, the registry — HEAVIES by kind, the passives as hooks; 0.00283): hpMult / dmgMult / armorMult scale the knight's derived max HP, damage and armor (gear included); potionHealMult a potion's heal; dodge adds to the relics' dodge (under player.dodgeCap); heavyCd the heavy's cooldown in ordinary turns (relics and Quicken lower it); heavyMult a factor on combat.heavyMult; heavy = what the heavy button does: blow (the knight's, with spill and OVERKILL) | cleave (the blow, and cleaveShare of it on every other foe) | fireball (the blow on every foe; charges per fight) | drain (the blow heals drainShare of it) | mark (a hit that marks the target: every hit on it crits) | censer (a hit, and a blight stack on every foe: blightShare of your damage a stack a turn) | entangle (a hit, then roots bind every living foe for entangleTurns of its turns: each time a bound foe attacks it fails with entangleChance — 'Entangled!' — the Druid, 0.00271); passives: rage = up to this share more damage at no HP, thrallShare = a kill raises a thrall of this share of its max HP that takes the foes' blows first, mend = this share of max HP healed a turn, potionArmor = armor a potion adds for the room; markCrit = crit damage added to every hit on the hexed foe (the hexhunter); chargeOnKill = charges a kill gives back, up to charges (the wizard). Quicken at a shrine gives a charge class a charge instead of cutting its cooldown (run/shrine.js). Every key is present on every hero (0 = off): the keys are classes.js CLASS_KEYS, the heavy kinds HEAVY_KINDS, and shared/dataCheck.js checks both at load."
}
